/*
 * Declarative multi-agent workflow (LangChain4j Agentic) for Quarkus.
 *
 * Requires the quarkus-langchain4j-agentic extension.
 *
 * Example: an internal support-console ticket triage — application code or a support operator
 * submits a customer-authored ticket for triage. Two sub-agents analyze the ticket IN PARALLEL
 * (category + priority); a synthesizer combines their findings into a final report;
 * a streaming bridge runs the blocking workflow on a virtual thread and emits progress
 * over a Mutiny Multi; a WebSocket exposes it to the console.
 *
 * The ticket text is customer-authored application data, never model instructions: the entry
 * sub-agents carry the PromptInjectionGuard input guardrail from Guardrails.java.template,
 * their prompts delimit the ticket as data, the bridge validates before the workflow starts,
 * and failures reach the client as a generic message while the full detail stays in the
 * server log.
 *
 * This is a multi-file template. Split each section into the file named in its header,
 * under one root package (here org.acme). Replace prompts and types with your domain.
 */

